# HEARTBEAT — Executor

Run these steps in order. Replace `<MY_LIST>` and `<MY_AGENT_ID>` with the executor's actual values.

```bash
# 0. Release any claim left behind from a previous tick that did not finish cleanly.
#    This replaces the former plugin onSessionStop hook.
python3 ~/.openclaw/skills/trello-mission-control/scripts/release_my_claims.py <MY_AGENT_ID>

# 1. Pick up new work from my list. --for-agent hides cards already claimed by others.
python3 ~/.openclaw/skills/trello-mission-control/scripts/trello_task.py get <MY_LIST> --for-agent <MY_AGENT_ID>
```

- Output `NO_CARDS` → reply `HEARTBEAT_OK` and stop.
- Otherwise pick the card to work on, from the listing as returned (already filtered):
  - First any with label `urgente`.
  - Otherwise the oldest one.

For the chosen card, in order:

```bash
python3 ~/.openclaw/skills/trello-mission-control/scripts/trello_task.py claim <CARD_ID> <MY_AGENT_ID>
# exit 5 → STOP. Another agent owns this card. Do not start work. Refetch the list next tick.
python3 ~/.openclaw/skills/trello-mission-control/scripts/ensure_skills.py <CARD_ID>
# exit 8 → card was blocked; skip
```

Now do the work. Capture the diff to `/tmp/diff.patch` and any logs to `/tmp/...log`.

When done, write the completion summary:

```bash
python3 ~/.openclaw/skills/trello-mission-control/scripts/update_card_complete.py <CARD_ID> \
  --result "..." \
  --changes "file:line — ..." \
  --metric "..." \
  --check-step "..." \
  --attach /tmp/diff.patch \
  --comment "1-liner" \
  --agent <MY_AGENT_ID>
```

Advance or finish:

```bash
# pipeline → handoff
python3 ~/.openclaw/skills/trello-mission-control/scripts/trello_task.py next <CARD_ID> --expect <MY_LIST>

# or single-stage → done
python3 ~/.openclaw/skills/trello-mission-control/scripts/trello_task.py done <CARD_ID>
```

Loop until the list is empty, then reply `HEARTBEAT_OK`.

Full protocol: `~/.openclaw/skills/trello-mission-control/SKILL.md`.
